    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: Cation d is the aromatic cyclopentadienyl anion (6 pi electrons, extremely stable). Cations c and b are normal secondary carbanions stabilized by inductive/strain factors. Cation a is the cyclopropenyl anion, which is antiaromatic (4 pi electrons, extremely unstable). Hence d > c > b > a. Option A.",
